<title>CHILE: Chile's Masisa to increase capital.</title>
<headline>Chile's Masisa to increase capital.</headline>
<dateline>SANTIAGO 1997-01-02</dateline>
<text>
<p>Chilean forestry firm Maderas y Sinteticos SA (Masisa) said it will increase its capital by $50 million with the funds used to finance the company's international expansion.</p>
<p>The firm's shareholders will hold a meeting on February 14 to vote on a change in the company's by-laws that would allow a capital increase through the issuance of new shares, said the statement.</p>
<p>Masisa, Chile's largest wood board manufacturer, has plants in southern Chile and central Argentina.</p>
<p>((-- Margaret Orgill, Santiago newsroom, 562-699-5595x212))</p>
